CS 252 Lab 2 – Shell Scripting
Student: Naman Kansal (kansal2)

FEATURES IMPLEMENTED

Part 1: Password Strength Checker
• Bash script to evaluate password strength using regular expressions
• Passwords accepted from command-line arguments and/or input file
• Scoring system based on character composition and patterns
• Validation of password length constraints
• Detection of required character classes:
  – Uppercase letters
  – Lowercase letters
  – Numbers
  – Special characters
• Penalties applied for:
  – Repeated characters
  – Consecutive lowercase sequences
  – Consecutive uppercase sequences
  – Consecutive numeric sequences
• Error messages printed for invalid password conditions
• Regex-based matching implemented using standard UNIX tools

Script: pwcheck.sh

---

Part 2: Directory Backup Utility
• Bash script to create versioned backups of a directory
• Backups stored using incremental sequence numbers
• Backup created only if directory contents have changed
• Detection of file changes using timestamps and directory comparison
• Automatic creation of backup directory if it does not exist
• Maximum number of backups enforced by removing oldest backups
• Recursive handling of nested subdirectories
• Error handling for invalid paths and failed commands
• Designed to be runnable via cron for automated daily backups

Script: backupdir.sh

---

Part 3: Process Information Monitor
• Bash script to display runtime information about active processes
• Processes filtered by command name pattern
• Information collected per process:
  – Process ID (PID)
  – Command name
  – User
  – Memory usage
  – CPU time
  – Number of threads
• Optional timed mode to refresh output at fixed intervals
• Process data extracted using:
  – ps for process discovery
  – /proc filesystem for detailed metrics
• Filtering logic to avoid false matches from command arguments
• Robust handling of missing or invalid input



Script: procinfo.sh

---

CONCEPTS DEMONSTRATED
• Bash scripting fundamentals
• Regular expressions in shell scripts
• File and directory manipulation
• Process monitoring using /proc
• UNIX command-line utilities
• Error handling in shell scripts
• Automation and cron-based execution

BUILDING AND RUNNING

Make scripts executable
chmod +x pwcheck.sh backupdir.sh procinfo.sh

Password Checker
./pwcheck.sh [-f passwordFile] [password1 password2 ...]

Backup Utility
./backupdir.sh <dir> <backup-dir> <max-backups>

Process Monitor
./procinfo.sh [-t seconds] pattern

